IMPORT prelude
IMPORT daydate
IMPORT `eia-core`
IMPORT `ei3-part3-account`

-- Tests of ei3-part3-account.l4 (Act ss 70.2 to 80.1).
-- Expected values are hand-worked from the text of the section named beside each assertion. Every figure is invented.

§ `s 70.2 the Account`

#ASSERT `s 70.2 the account established in the accounts of Canada` EQUALS `ei3 the Employment Insurance Operating Account`

§ `s 72 what is paid into the Consolidated Revenue Fund`

-- Paragraph (a): the listed kinds, when received under Parts I and III to IX.
#ASSERT `s 72 the amount is paid into the Consolidated Revenue Fund` `ei3 a premium` TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 72 the amount is paid into the Consolidated Revenue Fund` `ei3 a fine` TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 72 the amount is paid into the Consolidated Revenue Fund` `ei3 a penalty imposed under section 38, 39 or 65.1` TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 72 the amount is paid into the Consolidated Revenue Fund` `ei3 a penalty on benefit repayment` TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 72 the amount is paid into the Consolidated Revenue Fund` `ei3 a penalty of another kind` TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 72 the amount is paid into the Consolidated Revenue Fund` `ei3 interest under section 80.1` TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 72 the amount is paid into the Consolidated Revenue Fund` `ei3 interest on benefit repayment` TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 72 the amount is paid into the Consolidated Revenue Fund` `ei3 interest of another kind` TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 72 the amount is paid into the Consolidated Revenue Fund` `ei3 repayment of overpaid benefits` TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 72 the amount is paid into the Consolidated Revenue Fund` `ei3 benefit repayment` TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
-- Not received under those Parts: paragraph (a) says nothing (not covered).
#ASSERT `s 72 the amount is paid into the Consolidated Revenue Fund` `ei3 a premium` FALSE EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `s 72 the amount is paid into the Consolidated Revenue Fund` `ei3 benefit repayment` FALSE EQUALS NOTHING
-- Paragraphs (b) and (c) have no Part condition.
#ASSERT `s 72 the amount is paid into the Consolidated Revenue Fund` `ei3 an amount collected for services rendered to other government departments or agencies or to the public` FALSE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 72 the amount is paid into the Consolidated Revenue Fund` `ei3 principal or interest on a loan made by the Commission under Part II` FALSE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 72 the amount is paid into the Consolidated Revenue Fund` `ei3 repayment of an overpayment made by the Commission under section 61 for employment support measures` FALSE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 72 the amount is paid into the Consolidated Revenue Fund` `ei3 repayment of an overpayment made by the Commission under an agreement entered into under section 63` FALSE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 72 the amount is paid into the Consolidated Revenue Fund` `ei3 repayment of another overpayment made by the Commission under Part II` FALSE EQUALS JUST TRUE
-- A kind the section does not list.
#ASSERT `s 72 the amount is paid into the Consolidated Revenue Fund` `ei3 an amount of a kind these sections do not list` TRUE EQUALS NOTHING

§ `s 75 other credits to the Account`

-- Only amounts paid into the Consolidated Revenue Fund.
#ASSERT `s 75 the amount is credited to the Employment Insurance Operating Account` `ei3 repayment of overpaid benefits` FALSE EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `s 75 the amount is credited to the Employment Insurance Operating Account` `ei3 a penalty imposed under section 38, 39 or 65.1` TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 75 the amount is credited to the Employment Insurance Operating Account` `ei3 repayment of overpaid benefits` TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 75 the amount is credited to the Employment Insurance Operating Account` `ei3 an amount collected for services rendered to other government departments or agencies or to the public` TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 75 the amount is credited to the Employment Insurance Operating Account` `ei3 principal or interest on a loan made by the Commission under Part II` TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 75 the amount is credited to the Employment Insurance Operating Account` `ei3 repayment of an overpayment made by the Commission under section 61 for employment support measures` TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 75 the amount is credited to the Employment Insurance Operating Account` `ei3 repayment of an overpayment made by the Commission under an agreement entered into under section 63` TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 75 the amount is credited to the Employment Insurance Operating Account` `ei3 interest under section 80.1` TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
-- "Except interest and penalties on benefit repayment" in (a); premiums and fines are credited by other sections.
#ASSERT `s 75 the amount is credited to the Employment Insurance Operating Account` `ei3 a penalty on benefit repayment` TRUE EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `s 75 the amount is credited to the Employment Insurance Operating Account` `ei3 interest on benefit repayment` TRUE EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `s 75 the amount is credited to the Employment Insurance Operating Account` `ei3 a premium` TRUE EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `s 75 the amount is credited to the Employment Insurance Operating Account` `ei3 a fine` TRUE EQUALS NOTHING

§ `ss 73 to 74 credits`

-- 1,000 of premiums receivable + 200 appropriated + 50 of benefit repayments = 1,250.
#ASSERT `s 73 the amount credited to the Account and charged to the Consolidated Revenue Fund for the year` 1_000 200 50 EQUALS 1_250
#ASSERT `s 73 the amount credited to the Account and charged to the Consolidated Revenue Fund for the year` 0 0 0 EQUALS 0
#ASSERT `s 73.1 the day on which the amount is credited` EQUALS YMD 2010 8 1
#ASSERT `s 73.1 the day on which the budget was tabled in Parliament` EQUALS YMD 2009 1 27
#ASSERT `s 73.1 the cost of the benefit enhancement measures estimated in the budget` EQUALS 2_900_000_000
-- The amount credited is the Minister of Finance's determination, not the estimate.
#ASSERT `s 73.1 the amount credited to the Account on August 1, 2010` 2_850_000_000 EQUALS 2_850_000_000
#ASSERT `s 74 the amount credited to the Account and charged to the Consolidated Revenue Fund` 4_000_000 EQUALS 4_000_000

§ `ss 77 to 79 charges, special warrants, forecasts, cap, plan`

#ASSERT `s 77(1) the payment is charged to the Account` `ei3 amounts paid as or on account of benefits under this Act` EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 77(1) the payment is charged to the Account` `ei3 amounts paid under section 61 for employment support measures` EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 77(1) the payment is charged to the Account` `ei3 amounts paid under paragraph 63(1)(a)` EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 77(1) the payment is charged to the Account` `ei3 the costs of administering this Act, including administration fees or costs paid under section 62 or paragraph 63(1)(b)` EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 77(1) the payment is charged to the Account` `ei3 the costs of administering sections 28.1 and 28.2 of the Department of Employment and Social Development Act` EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 77(1) the payment is charged to the Account` `ei3 the costs of administering Part 5 of the Department of Employment and Social Development Act in respect of appeals respecting this Act` EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 77(1) the payment is charged to the Account` `ei3 a payment of a kind section 77(1) does not list` EQUALS NOTHING
-- Special warrants: benefits "shall"; sections 61 and 63(1)(a) "may"; nothing is said of the rest.
#ASSERT `s 77(2) the way the amount is paid by special warrant` `ei3 amounts paid as or on account of benefits under this Act` EQUALS JUST `ei3 shall be paid by special warrants`
#ASSERT `s 77(2) the way the amount is paid by special warrant` `ei3 amounts paid under section 61 for employment support measures` EQUALS JUST `ei3 may be paid by special warrants`
#ASSERT `s 77(2) the way the amount is paid by special warrant` `ei3 amounts paid under paragraph 63(1)(a)` EQUALS JUST `ei3 may be paid by special warrants`
#ASSERT `s 77(2) the way the amount is paid by special warrant` `ei3 the costs of administering Part 5 of the Department of Employment and Social Development Act in respect of appeals respecting this Act` EQUALS NOTHING
-- A special warrant is issued electronically OR bearing the printed signatures of the Chairperson and Vice-Chairperson.
#ASSERT `s 77(2) the special warrant is validly issued` TRUE TRUE FALSE
#ASSERT `s 77(2) the special warrant is validly issued` TRUE FALSE TRUE
#ASSERT `s 77(2) the special warrant is validly issued` TRUE TRUE TRUE
#ASSERT NOT (`s 77(2) the special warrant is validly issued` TRUE FALSE FALSE)
#ASSERT NOT (`s 77(2) the special warrant is validly issued` FALSE TRUE TRUE)
-- s 77(3): negotiable without charge at any financial institution in Canada.
#ASSERT `s 77(3) the special warrant is negotiable without charge at the institution` TRUE TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 77(3) the special warrant is negotiable without charge at the institution` TRUE FALSE EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `s 77(3) the special warrant is negotiable without charge at the institution` FALSE TRUE EQUALS NOTHING
-- s 77.1: on or before July 22 in the year.
#ASSERT `s 77.1 the day on or before which the forecasts and estimates are to be made` 2027 EQUALS YMD 2027 7 22
#ASSERT `s 77.1 the forecasts and estimates were made in time` 2027 (YMD 2027 7 22) (YMD 2027 7 1)
#ASSERT NOT (`s 77.1 the forecasts and estimates were made in time` 2027 (YMD 2027 7 23) (YMD 2027 7 1))
#ASSERT NOT (`s 77.1 the forecasts and estimates were made in time` 2027 (YMD 2027 7 1) (YMD 2027 7 23))
-- s 78: 0.8% of 1,000,000,000 is 8,000,000; "must not exceed" so exactly the maximum is allowed.
#ASSERT `s 78 the most that may be paid out under section 61 and paragraph 63(1)(a) in the fiscal year` 1_000_000_000 EQUALS 8_000_000
#ASSERT `s 78 the total paid out is within the maximum` 8_000_000 1_000_000_000
#ASSERT NOT (`s 78 the total paid out is within the maximum` 8_000_001 1_000_000_000)
#ASSERT `s 78 the total paid out is within the maximum` 0 1_000_000_000
-- s 79: submitting the plan and having it included in the Main Estimates.
#ASSERT `s 79 the Minister has done what the section requires` TRUE TRUE
#ASSERT NOT (`s 79 the Minister has done what the section requires` TRUE FALSE)
#ASSERT NOT (`s 79 the Minister has done what the section requires` FALSE TRUE)

§ `s 80.1 interest on amounts owing to Her Majesty`

#ASSERT `s 80.1(2) the interest is a debt due to Her Majesty` TRUE
#ASSERT NOT (`s 80.1(2) the interest is a debt due to Her Majesty` FALSE)
-- 72 months after 31 March 2020 is 31 March 2026: recovery on that day is not "more than 72 months after".
#ASSERT `s 80.1(3) the interest may still be recovered` (YMD 2020 3 31) (YMD 2026 3 31)
#ASSERT NOT (`s 80.1(3) the interest may still be recovered` (YMD 2020 3 31) (YMD 2026 4 1))
-- 72 months after 29 February 2020 clamps to 28 February 2026.
#ASSERT `s 80.1(3) the interest may still be recovered` (YMD 2020 2 29) (YMD 2026 2 28)
#ASSERT NOT (`s 80.1(3) the interest may still be recovered` (YMD 2020 2 29) (YMD 2026 3 1))
-- s 80.1(4): the carve-out is "other than Parts IV and VII"; for those the subsection says nothing.
#ASSERT `s 80.1(4) section 155.1 of the Financial Administration Act applies` FALSE EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `s 80.1(4) section 155.1 of the Financial Administration Act applies` TRUE EQUALS NOTHING
